  "loading_differences": [
    "Namespace-load emem and emem.embedding_model to avoid unused local-model eager imports. Namespace-load emem.evaluation to avoid unused LoCoMo evaluator downloading QA metric models.",
    "Alias original prompt template modules under the loader's legacy src.emem names, retaining one canonical package/class identity in subprocesses without changing template or loader bodies.",
    "Official BaseEmbeddingModel and stores unchanged; provider encode bridge uses public embedding service, upstream batch splitting and normalization.",
    "Official CacheOpenAI class, cache decorator, request scheduling, retries and reranking unchanged; supply public endpoint/key and meter SDK calls.",
    "Bind utils.config_utils.get_support_json_schema explicitly during import, construction and runtime reranking; temporarily bind structuring_openai's imported getter during construction. No process environment mutation; conflicting capability modes require isolated executor processes.",
    "Public completed tasks become new LoCoMo sessions. assistant role maps Doctor; other roles map Environment, original role retained in text. No upstream QA called.",
    "Snapshot exact native graph/OpenIE/contents/parquet; stable SQLite logical cache export. Native no-PPR placeholder scores are omitted from public rows.",
    "Retain original SQLite cache statements and transactions, close native context-manager connections at exit to release Windows handles. Use Windows extended paths and portable log filenames; original logging handlers and formatters remain.",
    "Supplement real task/output/feedback fields absent from provided events with attributed stable-ID events, never retrieved/applied context. Native trace tuple-key maps become tagged JSON key/value pairs without changing retrieval.",
    "Provider failures caught by native fallback code are surfaced after the operation for benchmark validity; native algorithm fallbacks for malformed generated content remain original."
  ],
  "source_setup": "python scripts/fetch-memory-adapter-source.py emem",
  "environment_setup": "Create a Python 3.12 virtual environment and pip install -r methods/emem/requirements-lock.txt; configure runtime.python_executable to that interpreter.",
